The positive admissible ratio-stratum theorem, relative analytic-rank proportion
bounds and positive absolute low-rank proportions are not statable at the pins:
they additionally need the actual isogeny-kernel character, its local twisting
comparison and the arithmetic Selmer-ratio family.

The nineteen-a3 admissible density and the local good-reduction obstruction for
y² + xy + 3y = x³ are scope diagnostics on single explicit curves, kept in
README.md as targets with their Checks; they are not headline theorems.
